From 78666e0b1d4c28bf3649642b5fb8640c68a1a254 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kudriavuy <169286443+kudriavuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:04:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] Live icons, sliders on keys, keyboard light slider,
 quieter pixel shift

Live = "Volume" / "Mic" makes a button's icon follow the session: the
helper's files /run/tiny-dfr/bridge/volume and .../mic (inotify) choose
one of VolumeIcons (muted, 0, up to half, more) or MicIcons (muted, on).

Slider = "Volume" / "Brightness" / "Keyboard" on a key with an Action:
held and slid it opens that slider (from where the value is, back to the
keys on release); tapped it sends its key on release instead of on touch,
so that a slide never sends it. Command = "KeyboardSlider" and the
keyboard-light slider: value from the kbd_backlight LED, "keyboard <v>" to
the helper, IllumUp/IllumDown without it. A slider whose button has no
room for the capsule on its left opens on its right.

Pixel shift no longer moves while the Touch Bar backlight is off (nothing
to protect, no frames), and PixelShiftSmooth = false moves one whole pixel
every 10 s instead of a 4 s sub-pixel animation of 20 full frames.

Local patch for MacBookPro13,2 (T1), not from upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream: https://github.com/AsahiLinux/tiny-dfr (applies to 285faff8b8cae893e9babd673b904929dd6f7f9c)
